      "question": "Figure 4 shows a closed curve with equation (x + y)^3 + 10y^2 = 108x. Show that dy/dx = (108 - 3(x + y)^2)/(20y + 3(x + y)^2).",
      "status": "ready",
      "answer": "dy/dx = (108 - 3(x + y)^2)/(20y + 3(x + y)^2) (shown)",
      "steps": [
        "Differentiate each term with respect to x, using the chain rule on (x + y)^3 and on 10y^2.",
        "3(x + y)^2 (1 + dy/dx) + 20y dy/dx = 108.",
        "Collect the dy/dx terms: dy/dx (3(x + y)^2 + 20y) = 108 - 3(x + y)^2.",
        "Divide by (3(x + y)^2 + 20y) to get the given result."
      ],
